==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
MHR (82).png|Uncontrollable Anger
CF (316).png|Low Intelligence
GF (241).png|Aquaphobia
CF (341).png|Distracted by Laser Pointers
FAtC (385).png|Sensitive Hearing
CF (92).png|Felikinesis Vulnerability
</gallery>
Rath's brain is hardwired for aggression and as such, Rath's main weakness is his lack of intelligence and highly aggressive temperament. This causes Rath to become easily distracted and difficult to stop once he starts fighting. He is also not quite adept for diplomatic approaches, particularly negotiations, and can make bad or difficult situations worse.<ref name="CoR" /> Additionally, opponents can defeat him if they exploit his lack of intelligence and single-minded aggression.<ref name="Catfight" />

Rath's apparent lack of intelligence also often convinces him to needlessly argue with inanimate objects.<ref name="PN775IM" />

Rath is scared of water, like most actual cats, but unlike actual tigers.<ref name="GF" />

Being a feline-based alien, Rath can be controlled by people that have the ability to control cats, like [[Nyancy Chan]]. He can also be easily distracted by a laser pointer.<ref name="Catfight" />

Rath has very sensitive hearing, which makes him vulnerable to loud piercing sounds, such as an [[Ultimate Sonorosian]]'s [[Sonic Disc|sonic discs]]<ref>''[[Double or Nothing]]''</ref> and certain [[Sonic Frequency Device|sonic frequency signals]].<ref name="FAtC" />

Rath can easily be scared by [[Toepick]]'s [[Toepick's Species|species]].{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick Can Scare Appoplexians.png]]|group = DJW}}

==History==
===Alien Force===
*Rath first appeared in ''[[Con of Rath]]'', where he was accidentally unlocked by [[Prince of Lewoda]], and [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] remained as said transformation until [[Zaw-Veenull]] and [[Cicely]] took the Prince away at the end. Ben then transformed into him a second time, telling [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] that "Rath wanted a word with him".
* In ''[[Primus (Episode)|Primus]]'', [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]] as Rath was defeated by [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]].
*In ''[[Above and Beyond]]'', Rath defeated [[Manny Armstrong|Manny]].
*In ''[[Vendetta]]'', Rath battled some [[Forever Knights]].
*In ''[[The Final Battle: Part 1]]'', [[Albedo|Negative]] Rath jumped out of the [[Rustbucket II]] to find [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]].

===Ultimate Alien===
*In ''[[Fame]]'', Rath was seen on TV.
*In ''[[Duped]]'', Rath spoke to [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] on the phone and destroyed the [[Forever Knights]]' [[Plasma Beam Tank]].
*In ''[[Hit 'Em Where They Live]]'', Rath defeated [[Rojo]] and [[Rojo's Gang|her gang]].
*In ''[[Hero Time]]'', Rath was beaten by [[Captain Nemesis]] in a race.
*In ''[[The Big Story]]'', Rath defeated [[SevenSeven]].
*In ''[[Prisoner Number 775 is Missing]]'', Rath failed to stop [[Prisoner 775]] from escaping in a stolen [[Plumber Ship]], but was able to make it crash by taking pieces of the ship apart.
*In ''[[Greetings From Techadon]]'', Rath defeated a [[Techadon Robot]].
*In ''[[Double or Nothing]]'', [[Albedo|Negative]] Rath battled [[Echo Echo]] but was defeated when the latter went [[Ultimate Echo Echo|Ultimate]].
*In ''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Ben 10/Generator Rex: Heroes United]]'', Rath saved [[Diane Farrah]] and her cameraman before [[Rex Salazar (Generator Rex)|Rex]] unsuccessfully cured him under the impression that Rath was an [[EVO (Generator Rex)|EVO]]. Later, Rath was defeated by [[Alpha]]. 
**Also, Rath appeared as one of the many aliens when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was explaining his story to Rex.
*In ''[[A Knight to Remember]]'', Rath fought the [[Flame Keepers' Circle]] [[Esoterica|members]] but failed to stop them from escaping in a truck.
*In ''[[Inspector 13]]'', Gwen as Rath defeated several Techadon Robots.

===Omniverse===  
*In ''[[It Was Them]]'', Rath battled [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]]'s [[Mutant Ant|mutant ants]].
*In ''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 2]]'', Rath fought [[Zed]] and was defeated by [[Khyber]].
*In ''[[Many Happy Returns]]'', Rath saved [[Madison (Omniverse)|Madison]] from a burning building. He then went back in to find her doll before being saved by Gwen and Kevin.
*In ''[[Gone Fishin']]'', Rath saved himself, [[Rook Blonko|Rook]], and [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]] from a waterfall.
*In ''[[The Frogs of War: Part 1]]'', Rath destroyed an [[Incursean Space Fighter]].
*In ''[[Food Around the Corner]]'', Rath defeated [[Poltroon]].
*In ''[[Return to Forever]]'', Rath defeated [[Tummyhead]].
*In ''[[Something Zombozo This Way Comes]]'', Rath battled the [[Circus Freaks (Classic)|Circus Freaks]], who eventually defeated him and shot him out of their cannon.
*In ''[[Catfight]]'', Rath tried to fight [[Nyancy Chan]], but was hypnotized to do her crimes with her. He later appeared three more times due to Nyancy using the [[Omnitrix Remote Control]].
*In ''[[Rook Tales]]'', Rath failed to take off [[Rook Ben|Young One]]'s tail.
*In ''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 2]]'', Rath and [[Lightning Volt]] battled Mad [[Way Big (Classic)|Way Big]].
*In ''[[The Secret of Dos Santos]]'', Rath defeated [[Exo-Skull]]. Because [[Skurd]] corrected an error with the Omnitrix, Rath was speaking Spanish and wearing clothes for the first time.
*In ''[[Malgax Attacks]]'', [[Albedo|Negative]] Rath briefly appeared before going [[Ultimate Rath|Ultimate]].
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Rath appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

===Mad Ben's Timeline=== 
*In ''[[And Then There Were None]]'', [[Mad Ben|Mad]] Rath chased after [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]], only to be defeated by [[Fourmungousaur]].

