==Etymology==
Rath's name is a misspelled version of "wrath", meaning fury and rage, referencing his attitude and fury-based powers.

==Trivia== 
*Rath is the third alien in '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]''' and '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''' to not be voiced by [[Dee Bradley Baker]]; the first being [[Alien X (Classic)|Alien X]] and the second being [[Ghostfreak]].  
**Ironically, [[Rath (Reboot)|his reboot counterpart]] is voiced by Dee.
*Rath is the second alien to stay in a whole episode due to an [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] malfunction; the first being [[Grey Matter (Classic)|Grey Matter]].
*Rath and [[Buzzshock (Classic)|Buzzshock]] are the only aliens to have been unlocked by electromagnetic interference.
*The [[Vreedle Brothers]] state that [[Appoplexian (Classic)|Appoplexian]]s such as Rath are much more aggressive and dimmer than [[Vreedle|they]] are.<ref name="CoR" />
*Whenever Rath executes wrestling moves, he names them after stars.<ref name="AaB" />
*Out of all of [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]'s aliens, [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] and [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] find Rath the most entertaining and amusing due to his mediocre intelligence, occasionally joking about him behind his back or out of his earsight.<ref name="PN775IM" />
*Appoplexians have an advanced sense of shame and typically wear clothes. However, Rath used to be naked all the time<ref name="FAtC" /> because of "a horrible error on the part of the [[Omnitrix]]" that was eventually fixed by [[Skurd]].<ref name="SoDS" /> This change eventually became permanent.{{Refn|[[:File:Rath Clothed Permanent.png]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Rath Clothed Permanent 2.png]]|group = DJW}}
*[[Madison (Omniverse)|Madison]] likes [[Brainstorm]] better than Rath.<ref name = "MHR"/>
*If [[Benzarro]] were to transform into Rath, he would be hairless.{{Refn|[[:File:Benzarro Rath is Hairless.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Rath's personality{{Refn|[[:File:Dwayne Came Up With Rath's Personality.PNG]]|group = DM}} and the wrestling moves he used in ''[[Above and Beyond]]''{{Refn|[[:File:Dwayne Named Rath's Wrestling Moves.png]]|group = ES}} were conceived by [[Dwayne McDuffie]].
*Rath's existence was first hinted at by Dwayne on March 29, 2009, when asked if there were any aliens similar to [[Blitzwolfer]], whom Ben had to struggle to control against [[Loboan (Classic)|Loboan]] savagery.{{Refn|[[:File:Anodites are energy beings.png]]|group = DM}}
*Rath was originally supposed to appear in ''[[Viktor: The Spoils]]'' to threaten [[Dr. Viktor|King Viktor]].{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/f/f6/VTS_Script_First_Draft_V1_with_Dwayne%27s_Edits.pdf ''Viktor: The Spoils'' Script First Draft with Dwayne McDuffie's Edits (First Version)]|group = script|name = first1}}
*Rath's personality is similar to that of [[Wikipedia:Marvel Comics|Marvel Comics]] superheroes [[Wikipedia:Wolverine (character)|Wolverine]] and the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hulk Hulk] due to all three of them having aggressive personalities. Additionally, Rath shares the Hulk's tendency to refer to himself in third person and low intelligence.
*Rath's catchphrase, "LEMME TELL YA SOMETHIN'!", appears to be a reference to Hulk Hogan's signature catch phrase, "Let me tell you something, brother".
*Rath is [[Eugene Son]],{{Refn|[[:File:Eugene Favorite Villain.PNG]]|group = ES}}{{Refn|[[:File:Eugene Favorite Alien 2.PNG]]|group = ES}} [[Paul Eiding]],{{Refn|https://preservetube.com/watch?v&#61;fpCyFUnfZlA|group =PE}} [[Ashley Johnson]],{{Refn|group=AJ|https://preservetube.com/watch?v&#61;4s8v7XQYpzs}} [[Charlotte McDuffie]],{{Refn|https://www.youtube.com/live/unaX1hKhOy4|group = CM}} [[Dan Riba]] and [[Yuri Lowenthal]]'s favorite Omnitrix alien,{{Refn|[[:File:Yuri's Favorite Alien.png]]|group = YL}} the latter of whom states that his love for the Appoplexian transformation is mostly because of [[John DiMaggio]]'s voice acting.

